Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area. It is not a listed building and is not covered by a tree preservation order.

Under the council's windows guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material (for example, timber to uPVC) or the pattern (for example, the glazing bar layout or opening style), you will likely need to apply. If you're replacing like-for-like, you may not need to, but I'd recommend confirming that before you start work.

I can't give a formal planning opinion on your specific proposal. If you tell me what the existing and proposed windows look like, I can help you work out whether an application is likely to be needed.
